Description: A track with hot cues loads at its first hot cue
 Mixxx's default "load at" mode is the intro start, which a rekordbox track
 does not have until Mixxx has analysed it, so every track loaded at 0:00,
 cues or not. CueControl now seeks a loaded track to its first hot cue (the
 lowest-numbered pad holding one; saved loops do not count), or, with no hot
 cue, to its main cue, which the import makes the first memory cue. A track
 with neither loads by the configured mode as before. Only the "Beginning"
 mode still means 0:00, which keeps the vinyl-control needle drop working.
 .
 The first version (r38) loaded at the earliest of the main cue and the hot
 cues. The first memory cue usually sits on the first beat, at about 0:00,
 so nearly every track still loaded at the start. The import puts the other
 memory cues on pads after all the rekordbox hot cues, so the lowest pad
 holding a hot cue is always a real hot cue when the track has one.
 .
 trackAnalyzed() applies the same rule when analysis finishes on a deck that
 has not been moved since the load: a track with no cues gets a main cue at
 its first sound from the silence analyser and moves there, and a track that
 loaded at a cue stays on it instead of following the intro start the
 analyser adds.
 .
 No existing test moves: the tests that load a track with cues on it use
 SeekOnLoadMode::MainCue with only a main cue, where the rule picks the main
 cue. New tests: CueControlTest.SeekOnLoadFirstHotcue and
 SeekOnLoadMainCueWithoutHotcues.
Author: Pioneered CI <pioneered-build@localhost>
Forwarded: no
---
